### Shell Context

**You should call this once AS-IS before using terminal**.

```nu
which | where type == 'external' | where path !~ '(?i)^c:\\windows' | where path !~ '(?i)\\WindowsApps\\' | get command | sort | to text | print; pwd | print; git branch --show-current | to text | print; git branch --sort=-committerdate | lines | first 8 | to text | print
```

### Nushell Extern-command Result Handling

Nushell provides much more powerful mechanisms for handling extern command result than bash's `2>&1`.

```nu
cargo build|complete|do {$in|to text|save -f temp\complete;print $in.exit_code;$in.stdout|lines|slice (-13)..-2|to text|print;print SERR;$in.stderr|lines|where {|l| $l !~ 'Compiling' and $l !~ 'LINK : warning'}|to text|print}
```

{{/if}}
